# Secrets and local runtime
.env
.agentcfg/auth.json
.agentcfg/sessions/
.agentcfg/models-store.json
node_modules/

# QM scratch. A single round leaves hundreds of MB here; the durable outcome of a run is
# the recorded verdict, not the wavefunctions.
runs/
*.gbw
*.tmp
**/xtbrestart
**/xtbtopo.mol
**/charges
**/wbo
*.xtboptok

# Deposits are tracked: they are the reviewer-facing evidence and the whole point of the
# repository accompanying the paper. 35 MB working tree, ~11 MB packed, largest file 3.3 MB.
# ORCA scratch that produced them is not tracked (see runs/).

# Graph Memory: the state and the per-attempt judgements are tracked, because the STRICT
# count and every claim resting on it have to be checkable from a clone. Regenerated views
# (the *.html / *.png network renders) are not — they come back from the tracked state.
graph/derived/*
!graph/derived/.gitkeep
graph/canonical/*.html
graph/canonical/*.png

# Evidence: the audited state, the timelines, the audit ledgers and Experience Memory are
# tracked — Experience Memory is one of the two memories the method is about, so a clone
# without it cannot check that half of the claim. Session transcripts, per-round loop
# scratch and anything holding an API key are not tracked.
evidence/state/loop/
evidence/chemical_messages.json
evidence/interventions*.json
evidence/**/KEY.private.json

# Pre-change asset snapshots are tracked: they are what an EVOLUTION_LOG entry is diffed
# against, so without them the ledger is unverifiable.

# Supplementary evaluation lanes: local corpora and run outputs, never vendored.
# The convention is that each lane keeps a tracked README stating its own criterion.
tsbench/*
!tsbench/README.md

# Experiments: the runner, the scored data and the generated report are tracked, because a
# reported number has to be re-derivable. Per-run scratch, live monitoring and single-host
# launch scripts are not — they describe one machine, not the experiment.
experiments/**/caches/
experiments/**/logs/
experiments/**/pass1/
experiments/**/start_*.sh
experiments/**/stop_*.sh
experiments/**/jobs*.json

# Byte-compiled
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Regenerated network views only. A blanket *.html rule is wrong here: the deposit
# reports under deposits/*/00_report/ are primary evidence and the first thing a reviewer
# opens, and they are .html too.
graph/**/network*.html
graph/**/strict_network*.html
graph/**/strict_network*.png
graph/**/accepted_network.html
results_showcase.html

.DS_Store
